From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:46:20 -0400
Subject: settings: a Stedding section in chrome://settings, one toggle per
 preference

chrome://settings/stedding is the first entry in the settings menu, carries
the Stedding mark, and holds one toggle per Stedding profile preference:
peek for links leaving a pinned tab's site, the command-bar hint on the new
tab page, and the most-visited shortcut row there. Everything defaults to
on; the section exists to turn behaviours off.

The preferences live in chrome/browser/ui/stedding/stedding_prefs.h, are
registered from RegisterBrowserUserPrefs, and are exposed to the settings
WebUI through the settings_private allowlist. Each has exactly one reader:
PeekNavigationThrottle (ShouldPeek's peek_enabled signal) and the
third-party new tab page (hidden attributes on the hint and the shortcut
row). Strings are literals for now, like the command bar's.

Why: ROADMAP M5 asks for a settings surface; docs/features/settings.md
defines it.
Removable when: never, unless Stedding stops having preferences.
